            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of ultrasonic diagnosis and incidence of appendectomy and laparoscopy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1117-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A total of 330 of 409 patients with suspected acute appendicitis were examined by ultrasound, and an appendectomy was performed in 146 patients. The negative appendectomy rate was 7% with preoperative ultrasound (n = 72) compared with 31% without (n = 74). Laparoscopy did not reduce the negative appendectomy rate, but was useful in patients with opposing clinical and sonographical findings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
